WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.5 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Data collection, ethics and data quality

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Collect data ethically from the first day, using the simplest method you can keep up.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.133
Data collection is how you gather the evidence for each indicator: the method, the tools and the routine. It must be simple enough to keep up, ethical from the first day and reliable enough to trust.

4
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:29.133
Three things to get right

5
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:40.093
Simple methods: The simplest method that gives credible evidence: registers, surveys, interviews, observation, sales records. For example: A paper attendance sheet at the bakery training, filled in every morning.

6
00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:51.793
Ethics: Explain why, ask for consent, collect only what you need and keep it confidential. For example: Trainees sign a short consent note; their details stay in a locked folder.

7
00:00:51.793 --> 00:01:02.841
Quality: Valid, reliable, timely, precise and unchanged, protected by simple routine checks. For example: Each month the founder checks five sheets against the sign-up list.

8
00:01:03.241 --> 00:01:03.841
Why it matters

9
00:01:03.841 --> 00:01:09.515
1. Your evidence is only as good as the data behind it.

10
00:01:09.515 --> 00:01:15.189
2. People trust you with their information; losing that trust is costly.

11
00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:22.233
3. A routine you can keep up beats a perfect plan you abandon.

12
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:23.233
What it supports

13
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:29.278
1. Every indicator on your reference sheet gets a method and a tool.

14
00:01:29.278 --> 00:01:35.322
2. Your MEAL plan sets who collects, when, and how it is checked.

15
00:01:35.322 --> 00:01:41.626
3. Your monitoring and evaluation depend on this data being right.

16
00:01:42.026 --> 00:01:42.626
What to avoid

17
00:01:42.626 --> 00:01:48.670
An app nobody opens instead of a sheet that gets filled in.

18
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:54.715
Collecting extra personal data, or ignoring the data rules where you work.

19
00:01:54.715 --> 00:02:01.759
Skipping a test of your tools with a few real users first.

20
00:02:02.359 --> 00:02:04.159
You draft your data collection plan and quality checks.

21
00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:08.159
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:12.759
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
